    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0282" n="1116" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/273a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-25T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 25, 1918—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. We are giving to the press within next few days full schedule of commodities
                    and substance of our proposal of December 20, containing, however, no intimation
                    of that which has been offered or proposed to the United States by
                        Norway.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d252-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d252-f1" n="1" xml:id="d252-f1-content">
                <p>For the War Trade Board’s statement, see <hi rendition="#italic">The Official
                        Bulletin</hi>, Washington, Jan. 28, 1918 (vol. 2, No. 219), pp. 13 and
                    15–16.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
